# Frontend Performance — framework-agnostic

## Web Vitals targets (4G mid-range)
LCP ≤ 2.5 s · FCP ≤ 1.5 s · INP ≤ 200 ms · TBT ≤ 200 ms · CLS ≤ 0.1 · TTFB ≤ 800 ms.

## Bundle budgets
Critical path ≤ 180 KB gz · per-route chunk ≤ 80 KB gz. Fail CI when over.

## Code splitting & loading
- Lazy-load routes; dynamic-import heavy libs at usage site.
- Preload next probable route on hover/focus.
- `<link rel="modulepreload">` for critical chunks; `<link rel="preconnect">` to API/CDN.
- Third-party scripts use `async`/`defer` and load only where needed.

## Tree-shaking
- Named imports only (`import { x } from "lodash-es"`).
- `"sideEffects": false` for pure packages. Dedup deps via pnpm + Turborepo.

## Images & fonts
- Explicit `width` / `height` (CLS).
- Hero media may use `loading="eager"` + `fetchpriority="high"`; do not apply broadly.
- `loading="lazy"` + `decoding="async"` below the fold. AVIF/WebP with fallback.
- SVG icons inlined. Fonts: max two families, `font-display: swap`, preload only critical weight/style, subset glyphs.

## Animation
- Animate `transform`/`opacity` first; avoid layout-bound properties.
- Use `will-change` narrowly and remove it when animation finishes.
- CSS for simple transitions; approved animation libs or `requestAnimationFrame` for JS motion.

## Real-time render budget
- ~30 fps non-game UIs, 60 fps for canvases.
- Batch high-rate updates (>10 Hz) via `requestAnimationFrame`.
- Drop oldest non-critical frames past buffer threshold.

## Defensive UI
- "Reconnecting" banner; last-known-good values with `aria-busy="true"`.
- Queue or fail optimistic actions when socket is down.
